20,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
21,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
22,2,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
23,2,,status,Sakura,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
24,2,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"It seems our staffing is precarious. The late-turn pool is thinning, and overtime is covering both final departures and overnight works. We are stretched far too thin.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"Interesting. The old accessibility programme had mixed results with lane priority, but the late-evening pilot from eight years ago actually met its cost-recovery targets.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"My findings are concerning. Pre-war shells have unrecorded voids causing weeks of delays, and the ferry and rail offices can't even agree on passenger data terms.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The capital ledger has a lapsed grant balance, but the operating and technology lines were trimmed. Also, ticketing fees are now higher than our resurfacing budget.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"I found something weird! Mid-city runs take longer now, but crowds clear at the same rate. Also, people spend more time waiting for connections than paying.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Takumi, if the late-evening pilot worked, we should consider it, but only if we can find the staff to run it. My data says we have none.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, that's a fair point. But we should also note that lane-priority projects in the past were often returned to mixed traffic. We should avoid that.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Sakura, if the delays are in the connections and not the payment process, then a new ticketing system might not actually solve the passengers' main frustration.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with Toshio. If the technology budget is being trimmed, spending more on a complex fare platform seems risky given the contractor fees.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Toshio, you're right! If the queues at machines are short, the ""problem"" isn't the ticketing. It's the actual movement and the waiting.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Daisuke, the fact that the technology line was trimmed makes me even more worried about any plan requiring new systems or heavy maintenance.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"We need something that actually stays finished. If lane priority failed before, a bus corridor might just be another project that gets reverted.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Toshio,,And any work in the old stations is a gamble. Those unrecorded voids in the pre-war shells make station upgrades a potential nightmare for the schedule.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I just don't want us to commit to something that creates a huge debt in the following years. The paving rates are climbing too.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Sakura,,So we need something that fixes the actual time loss but doesn't rely on the things that are broken or too expensive!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
