48,3,,status,Sakura,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
49,3,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
50,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Looking at the candidates, the Night Service Extension is tempting because of the pilot, but the roster books show we have no one left to work.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Takumi,,The Crosstown Bus Corridor risks the same failure as the previous lane-priority stretches. I'm not sure it's a reliable bet.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Station Access Upgrades are too dangerous. The contingency pricing for pre-war shells suggests we'll hit voids and stall for weeks.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The Integrated Fare Platform seems expensive, and since the technology budget is trimmed and ticketing fees are high, I'm hesitant.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"If the problem is waiting for connections and mid-city slowness, the Bus Corridor might help, but the Fare Platform doesn't fix the time loss.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, the Bus Corridor requires roadway crews, and they are a third below establishment. We can't build what we can't maintain.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, what about the Night Service? If the pilot worked, maybe we can adjust the rosters instead of just adding more people?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the Night Service requires maintenance windows. But the late-turn pool is already covering overnight works. It's a recipe for burnout.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think the Fare Platform is the only one that doesn't require paving or construction, which avoids the climbing paving rates.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"But @Daisuke, the journey audits show that paying isn't where the minutes go! It wouldn't actually help the passengers' travel time.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I'm torn. But the maintenance contract for lifts and escalators actually has spare capacity. That makes Station Access Upgrades slightly more feasible.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, but Toshio found that the pre-war shells are full of surprises. Spare crew capacity doesn't help if the ground is a void.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Toshio,,Exactly. The only plan that avoids the physical risks of the shells and the staffing crisis of the night shifts is the Fare Platform.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"If the other three are impossible due to staff or ground risks, maybe the Fare Platform is the safest, even if the budget is tight.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"I still hate that it doesn't fix the crowding or the time, but if the others will just stall or fail, I guess it's the most realistic.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. Given the staffing shortages in the late-turn pool and roadway crews, the Fare Platform is the only one we can actually implement.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"It's not the most exciting, but it avoids the ""reverted to mixed traffic"" fate of the bus lanes. I'll go with the Fare Platform.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"It avoids the pre-war shell voids and the joint operator data conflicts are a hurdle, but not a physical impossibility. I vote for D.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I feel safer with a plan that doesn't involve climbing paving rates or construction risks. I vote for the Integrated Fare Platform.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Sakura,,I'll vote for the Fare Platform too. It's better than a plan that never gets finished because the crews are too tired!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
